# PrismNet services: the servers inetd starts when a connection comes in.
# As ENVARC:PrismNet/services (the installer's server options put one
# there; copy it to ENV:PrismNet too, or reboot), PrismNet starts inetd as
# soon as it is up and stops it with PrismNet STOP. Delete the file and no
# server runs. One service a line:
#
#   name  port  tcp  program  [arguments...]
#
# ftp: PrismNet's FTP server. Logins are PrismNet's users (PrismNet Prefs >
# Users); "/" shows the Amiga's volumes. Options:
#   ANONYMOUS=dir     also let "anonymous" in, read-only, inside dir only
#   READONLY          nobody may change anything
#   PASVPORTS=a-b     ports for passive transfers (for a firewall rule)
#   PASVADDRESS=ip    address to announce for passive transfers (behind NAT)
#   IDLE=seconds      drop an idle connection (default 600)
#
ftp  21  tcp  C:ftpd
#ftp  21  tcp  C:ftpd ANONYMOUS=Work:Public
#
# telnet: an AmigaDOS Shell over the network, in the user's home directory
# (PrismNet Prefs > Users). Telnet sends passwords as plain text: use it on
# your own network only. Options:
#   IDLE=seconds      drop an idle session (default 1800)
#   NOLOGIN=user      no login prompt, everyone is that user (trusted LAN only)
#
#telnet  23  tcp  C:telnetd
#
# http: a small web server - the files of one folder, read-only, no login.
# A folder's index.html is its page; without one the folder is listed.
# Options:
#   ROOT=dir          the folder served as "/" (default SYS:WWW)
#   INDEX=name        a folder's own page (default index.html)
#   NOLIST            no listings: a folder without its page is refused
#   IDLE=seconds      close an idle connection (default 15)
#   LOG=file          append one line per request (address, request, status, bytes)
#
#http  80  tcp  C:httpd ROOT=SYS:WWW
